  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "authoritative-android-insets",
      "finding": "The shared adapter reads actual Android View/decor/system-bar/cutout geometry on the Android UI thread and defers its result to Godot. It is byte-identical to the prior Cards adapter except for the comment naming the shared cache. Confirmed observations are scaled once; CreativeRuntime and Kart skip the origin-zero Godot max operation when the Android observation path is authoritative."
    },
    {
      "topic": "cache-and-rotation",
      "finding": "Request generation and request identity are checked before clearing pending state. Window changes and application pause/resume invalidate the cache. A delayed result for an older window/generation cannot replace a newer observation or release its pending flag. Same-size 180-degree changes are still read by the bounded 0.20-second poll and emit only when actual raw values change."
    },
    {
      "topic": "no-steady-state-layout-loop",
      "finding": "The observation dictionary is compared before emitting safe_area_changed. Cards no longer owns a second JNI poll. Unchanged observations do not repeatedly relayout card meshes or invalidate their settled diagnostic file. This is a source-level bounded-work finding, not a measured Android CPU/GPU budget."
    },
    {
      "topic": "scene-exit-and-deferred-layout",
      "finding": "Jump/creative/Cards and the additional consumers disconnect their signals before runtime restoration. Relevant layout entry points guard tree membership. Build deferred camera/goal layouts and Puzzle pre-await menu fitting now reject exited-but-still-alive nodes. The regression queues those real callbacks, removes scenes without immediately freeing them, and emits again."
    },
    {
      "topic": "additional-consumers",
      "finding": "Learning, Boot, Garage, Workshop, Kart, Settlement and Rhythm now use their existing callbacks for asynchronous inset changes. Existing parent Kart safe-area metadata remains in effect, avoiding a second inset in nested Garage/Workshop. The public UI helper resolves the scene-tree autoload and removes its bound callback at tree exit."
    },
    {
      "topic": "original-function-scope",
      "finding": "Compared modified production paths against the supplied, hash-matched 796b copies. Existing changes outside Cards are layout/cache subscriptions and lifecycle guards; existing game/save/question functions are not replaced. The exact 796b Puzzle menu fix is retained."
    },
    {
      "topic": "settled-cards-contract",
      "finding": "The six telemetry functions listed below remain byte-identical to the previously reviewed Cards freeze. Input acceptance and layout changes invalidate the prior file; publication waits for visible UI, no pending request, two settling frames, zero camera-focus offset and completed hand tweens. The actual mesh corners/public state/window and Android observation are atomically written through a temporary file; teardown removes both files. Shared cache values preserve the schema and fixture-vs-Android distinction."
    },
    {
      "topic": "additive-ci",
      "finding": "Read the full validate_studio.sh and exact diff. All eleven original probe invocations and original thirty PNGs remain, with their original budgets. Three headless and two rendered calls add Cards/adapter/shared checks. The roster requires thirty-seven PNGs, including the four exact 2400x1080 shared names and actual Cards layout sidecars. The existing strict run_godot_probe.py path is retained."
    }
  ],
